Subject: Compiled code parks a value whose last reference goes without three calls

What this does
  - `qjs_aot_drc_zero(ctx, v)` is JS_FreeValue for a counted value whose count is 1: it drops the
    count and, at zero, parks the value with `js_drc_zero` directly when no reconcile or collection
    is running, and through `js_free_value_rt` otherwise.

Why we need it
  The inline free of a compiled field store ends in JS_FreeValue -> JS_FreeValueRT ->
  js_free_value_rt -> js_drc_zero whenever the old value's count is 1, which on a call-heavy program
  is several times per loop iteration and about 57 instructions each. The decision those three calls
  make is the one `qjs_aot_drc_zero` makes in one.

Functions touched
  `qjs_aot_drc_zero` (new).

No.

--- a/quickjs.c
+++ b/quickjs.c
@@ -65221,0 +65222,18 @@
+/* Compiled code dropped a reference to a counted value whose count is 1: what JS_FreeValue does
+   for it, with the zero case going straight to the parking of the value. */
+void qjs_aot_drc_zero(JSContext *ctx, JSValue v)
+{
+    JSRuntime *rt = ctx->rt;
+    void *p = JS_VALUE_GET_PTR(v);
+
+    if (--JS_REF_COUNT(p) > 0)
+        return;
+#if QJS_DRC
+    if (likely(!rt->drc_in_reconcile && rt->gc_phase == JS_GC_PHASE_NONE)) {
+        js_drc_zero(rt, v);
+        return;
+    }
+#endif
+    js_free_value_rt(rt, v);
+}
+
--- a/quickjs-aot-rt.h
+++ b/quickjs-aot-rt.h
@@ -386,0 +387,4 @@
+/* The last reference of a counted value whose count is 1 goes: JS_FreeValue without its
+   intermediate calls. */
+void qjs_aot_drc_zero(JSContext *ctx, JSValue v);
